<title>BRAZIL: Bovespa sees 193.89 mln real net inflow March 1-10.</title>
<headline>Bovespa sees 193.89 mln real net inflow March 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange (Bovespa) said it registered foreign capital inflows of 193.89 million reais in the first 10 days of March.</p>
<p>Foreign purchases amounted to 1.067 billion reais, against foreign sales of 873.07 million reais.</p>
<p>So far this year, net foreign capital inflows to the Bovespa have totalled 1.036 billion reais. In February, net inflows amounted to 842.63 million reais.</p>
<p>Only stock is traded on the Bovespa.</p>
<p>((-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
